                <pb facs="0164" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg36"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 19.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lee to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 4,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Lee reports that the minister for foreign affairs has declared that he cannot
                    receive Mr. Keiley, and has asked that the United States appoint another
                    minister.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
